    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.misc\n\n### Description\n\nUsing `setup_termbg_sync` alongside firenvim breaks the latter because how it's designed to communicate with the browser.\r\n\r\nMy feature request is to add a FAQ or mention of taking this into account for end users of mini.misc.\r\n\r\nSaid FAQ could mentoin that to solve this issue a user simply has to conditionally enable `setup_termgb_sync` only if the current Neovim session hasn't been started by firenvim:\r\n\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    if not vim.g.started_by_firenvim then require(\"mini.misc\").setup_termbg_sync() end\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr do you think this should be mentioned on the firenvim side?",
    "closed_at": "2024-08-04T08:10:34Z",
