        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe general idea of the note about when it should be used sounds reasonable. I thought that having the mention of \"terminal emulator\" would be enough, but it might not be. There is now a [dedicated note](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/af673d8523c5c2c5ff0a53b1e42a296ca358dcc7/doc/mini-misc.txt#L187) on latest `main`.\r\n\r\nMentioning any specific cases of when *not* to call it (like when Firenvim is used, etc.) seems to be too much.",
